config BR2_PACKAGE_INGENIC_MUSL_SHIM
	bool "ingenic-musl-shim"
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_USES_MUSL
	help
	  The libc symbols Ingenic's libimp.so and libalog.so were linked
	  against and musl does not define.

	  The vendor libraries are uClibc builds, so they leave
	  __assert, __fgetc_unlocked, __pthread_register_cancel and
	  __pthread_unregister_cancel undefined as strong references. On a
	  musl image nothing resolves them, and the program that loads
	  libimp fails at relocation rather than at a call site.

	  Static archive, staging only: the consumer links it with
	  --whole-archive --export-dynamic so the symbols are exported from
	  the executable, which is where the vendor library looks for them.

	  https://github.com/gtxaspec/ingenic-musl
